      "backstory": {
        "description": "Dr. Voss is a professor of ancient history and Near Eastern archaeology at Miskatonic University. She has led three expeditions to the Middle East and one ill-fated trip to a dig site in rural England that she refuses to discuss.",
        "personalDescription": "Sharp-eyed woman with ink-stained fingers and an air of perpetual mild impatience.",
        "ideology": "Knowledge is its own justification. The universe is vast and strange — hiding from that fact helps no one.",
        "significantPeople": "Professor Harold Crane, her mentor; now deceased under unexplained circumstances.",
        "meaningfulLocations": "The Orne Library at Miskatonic — where she first encountered a text she wishes she had never read.",
        "treasuredPossessions": "A scarab amulet of uncertain origin, found at the English dig site. She keeps it in a locked box.",
        "traits": "Methodical; slow to trust; rarely panics in the field — though she's been having bad dreams lately.",
        "injuriesAndScars": "A faint scar across the left palm from broken glass at the English dig site.",
        "phobiasAndManias": "Mild irrational dread of deep water following a childhood incident.",
        "arcaneTomesAndSpells": "Has read portions of a text she believes to be a corrupt Latin translation of something older; this accounts for her 3% Cthulhu Mythos.",
        "encountersWithStrangeEntities": "Witnessed what she described in her journal only as 'the outline of something that should not have been there' at the England dig site."
      },

